-- title:
--   Each branch ideal at a crossing equals (a,q)
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a non-zero natural number and $q$ a prime with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of the structure `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, packaging the integral model `X N₀ q` over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the base ring `DRLevel.R q` (proper, flat, integral, locally of finite presentation, with integrally closed affine sections) together with its generic-fibre identification with a curve model of the modular function field of level $N_0q$, its smoothness and geometric integrality in the generic fibre, and the two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ over the base. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O : \mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q \to O$ whose maximal ideal is $\operatorname{span}\{q\}$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$, and let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 0$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 1$; write $x_n = \mathfrak X.\mathrm{crossingPt}\ \rho_O\ \mathrm{to}\kappa\ n$ for its image in $\mathrm{XO}\ \rho_O$ under the first projection followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O)\ 0$ and the base-change map $\mathrm{bcMap}\ \rho_O\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$. Assume that the points $\mathfrak X.\xi_\infty$ and $\mathfrak X.\xi_0$ of $\mathrm{XO}\ \rho_O$ each specialise to $x_n$, giving the two branch ideals $\mathrm{branchIdeal}$, i.e. the preimages under the specialisation maps of stalks of the maximal ideals of the stalks at $\xi_\infty$, resp. $\xi_0$, inside $R = \mathcal O_{\mathrm{XO}\,\rho_O,\,x_n}$. Let $\varpi \in R$ be $\mathrm{baseGerm}$ of $q$, the germ at $x_n$ of the global section obtained from $q \in O$ through the structure morphism $\mathrm{XO.toBase}\ \rho_O$. Then there exist $a \in R$ with $\operatorname{span}\{a,\varpi\}$ equal to the branch ideal at $\xi_\infty$, and $b \in R$ with $\operatorname{span}\{b,\varpi\}$ equal to the branch ideal at $\xi_0$.
--
--   This records that at a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ each of the two branch ideals in the local ring of the crossing point is generated by the germ of the uniformiser $q$ together with a single further element, the local shape used to produce oriented charts at crossings; it is cited by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart).
